WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.876
♪ (UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.003
Welcome back.
And thank you for joining us

00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:05.588
for another episode
of the Wine Down.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:08.842
We are joined today
by the incredible Yvonne Orji.

00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:09.843
-Hey.
-Oh, hello.

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:13.138
-Was that the DMX voice? Hey.
-No, no.

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:14.597
It's never the DMX voice.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.015
I'm ready.

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:17.183
-You're ready.
-I'm always.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.060
And we are ready
to dig into episode two,

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.353
which is "Lowkey Distant."

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:22.689
ALL: Oof. (LAUGHING)

00:00:22.772 --> 00:00:25.608
♪ (MUSIC CONTINUES) ♪

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.695
-So Molly met Condola...
-Uh-huh.

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:29.821
...for the first time...

00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:30.864
-Yes.
-...this episode.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:32.866
And it was a little awkward
encounter.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.328
How does Molly feel about, uh,
Condola and Issa's friendship?

00:00:37.579 --> 00:00:38.913
Well I don't know
how Molly feels about Condola,

00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:40.248
but I know how Molly feels
about Issa.

00:00:40.331 --> 00:00:41.833
-Whoa.
-And she is trying

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:44.210
to protect her friendship.
And she just feels like,

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:47.046
as messy as Molly is,
she sees the messiness.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.590
Like, this ain't gonna work.

00:00:48.673 --> 00:00:50.175
But she's so nice.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.426
They all are.

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:52.552
-It is that thing though...
-I mean,

00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:53.845
it's always the nice ones
you gotta watch out for.

00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:56.431
But you don't think
that there's any jealousy

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:59.851
rooted in Molly's interactions
with them,

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.103
in her POV of Condola?
Because...

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:03.813
Condola has been around a lot,

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.441
and has been occupying
a lot of Issa's time.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:09.319
(STAMMERS)
Is Yvonne also jealous?

00:01:09.527 --> 00:01:10.487
(LAUGHS)

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.739
Molly is not the jealous type,
but I ain't gonna front,

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:14.365
when we were shooting this
I was like, "Uh...

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:15.450
Why this ho still here?"

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:16.910
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:01:16.993 --> 00:01:18.244
And it's also like this thing
where--

00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:19.704
It's like when you know
your friend.

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:20.789
-YVONNE ORJI: Yes.
-And you're like,

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.749
"I know this is not
gonna end well."

00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:24.000
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.252
"So why--"
I'm trying to help you--

00:01:26.336 --> 00:01:27.587
-Let's fast forward the process.
-But you--" Yes.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.923
So what do you think
is going through Issa's mind

00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:32.592
when Lawrence tells her
that he likes Condola

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:34.469
and he wants it to work out
with her?

00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:36.846
You know, I think that's when
it becomes kind of real.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.600
It was real when Condola
dropped the news,

00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:42.852
you know, last episode.
And I think here,

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:44.395
it's just like,
he's saying he likes her,

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:46.439
and he wants to--
He really wants

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:49.275
to make an effort
to not have anything cloud

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.985
-cloud her view of him.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:54.531
And I think it hits her
in a realization way,

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.158
but I don't think that she has
fully processed

00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:58.535
what that means just yet.

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:01.412
The thing about Condola is
like she knows your weaknesses.

00:02:01.704 --> 00:02:03.665
So in some way
it's like Lawrence, like,

00:02:03.748 --> 00:02:06.292
got his life together
and they're great

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.460
and she's great
and it's like,

00:02:07.544 --> 00:02:09.879
"I'm over here asking her
for help?"

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.881
ALL: Oof.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.675
That's real. I'm done.

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:15.718
-Yvonne. Now, in this episode,
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:18.596
Andrew has a hard time
sort of opening up to Molly.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.598
-He does.
-Why do you think that is?

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:24.310
I don't know if it's that
he is, like,

00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:25.603
fear of commitment
but it's weird,

00:02:25.687 --> 00:02:27.605
because he pushes in
as if, like,

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:28.773
-"I'm ready to commit."
-Yeah.

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:30.108
And then it's like
he pulls back.

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:31.359
So that's what's kind
of frustrating

00:02:31.442 --> 00:02:32.861
and annoying to Molly,
because it's like,

00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:34.654
"Are we in it, are we--"
It's like we're double dutching.

00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:37.031
I also think too, I think
it's also a very guy thing

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:40.451
to like, in last season,
he was hunting her...

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:41.703
-Yes.
-...where it's like a chase.

00:02:41.786 --> 00:02:43.830
It's like she's rebuffing me,
now I'm obsessed.

00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:45.790
And then he kind of got her,
and then he was a little bit

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:47.834
like, "What you mean,
I gotta open up now?"

00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:50.253
"I'm-- I'm just trying to fuck
and have fun with you a lot.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.337
Like what's the problem?
Why we gotta talk?"

00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:54.382
♪ Such is the problem
With dating ♪

00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:55.675
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:02:55.758 --> 00:02:57.927
So in the spirit
of this episode,

00:02:58.428 --> 00:03:00.263
what do you do
when your best friend

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.806
is getting closer
to someone else?

00:03:02.307 --> 00:03:04.267
Hmm. Well there's some people
I know in Nigeria

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.769
that I can call and like
make people disappear.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.104
-So...
-(LAUGHS)

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.189
So you kill them?
Murder is your answer?

00:03:10.273 --> 00:03:11.608
-(CHUCKLES) I said disappear.
-Oh.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.359
I watch Investigation Discovery,
there's a big difference.

00:03:13.443 --> 00:03:15.278
-You know this is on camera.
-What?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.322
-Okay.
-(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:03:18.823 --> 00:03:22.243
Uh, I'm a dude. Dudes don't
really get like all--

00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:24.203
-I'm trying to think of a time--
-ORJI: Are you sure?

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:25.538
I don't think I've ever
been mad like--

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:27.582
If a dude that you don't like
is coming around--

00:03:27.665 --> 00:03:31.419
Yes, that is annoying.
Like if Condola was like,

00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:35.173
actually real annoying
and real disruptive,

00:03:35.256 --> 00:03:37.467
like I had a buddy of mine
that would always bring--

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.093
We'd go to Vegas
and he'd always invite

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:41.054
eight other people.
And I'm just like, "Bro..."

00:03:41.137 --> 00:03:42.388
-Oof.
-That's not it.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.723
That's not it.

00:03:44.015 --> 00:03:47.769
Yeah, for me,
I have blended friend groups,

00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:49.562
and that's all well and good
with me.

00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:51.064
Just don't leave me out.

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:52.649
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.025
-If you start leaving me out...
-Yes.

00:03:54.108 --> 00:03:55.401
-Now we have a problem.
-...we have a problem.

00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:57.320
I think just watching you
and your friendships,

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:01.199
you've been really good
at making everybody feel...

00:04:01.491 --> 00:04:03.076
connected.
Like you're loyal.

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.578
Like your loyalty and friendship
is very admirable.

00:04:05.662 --> 00:04:07.914
Until they leave me out
of some shit, and then...

00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:09.499
They gon' learn. (CHUCKLES)

00:04:09.832 --> 00:04:11.250
-Okay.
-Hey.

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:14.337
Well thank you all so much
for Wining Down with us.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.839
We can't wait to see you again
next week.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.591
Cheers.

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:19.592
-I mean I'm gonna drink.
-Yeah.

00:04:19.676 --> 00:04:20.677
I mean we usually get drinks.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.970
(ALL LAUGHING)

00:04:22.053 --> 00:04:24.180
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

